      "message": "The logic LGTM, but I think this could be written more clearly - the three nested ifs are IMO quite hard to understand.\n\nCould you pull some of this logic up into the switch statement? So put the early return in `BTM_SEC_OK`:\n```\n    case BTM_SEC_OK:\n      LOG_DEBUG(\"Security met\");\n      p_callback(\u0026bd_addr, BT_TRANSPORT_LE, p_ref_data, BTM_SUCCESS);\n      return L2CAP_LE_RESULT_CONN_OK;\n```\n\nThen in the PENDING case,\n```\n    case BTM_SEC_ENC_PENDING:\n      LOG_DEBUG(\"Ecryption pending\");\n      if (FLAG) {\n        // enqueue ourselves\n        BTM_SetEncryption(bd_addr, BT_TRANSPORT_LE, p_callback, p_ref_data, BTM_BLE_SEC_NONE);\n      }\n      return L2CAP_LE_RESULT_CONN_OK;\n```\n\nWe\u0027d group these two cases (OK + PENDING) at the start, and leave the other cases for later.\n\nAnd then after the switch statement, we\u0027d just have:\n```\nASSERT(ble_sec_act !\u003d BTM_BLE_SEC_NONE) {\nBTM_SetEncryption(...)\n}\n```\n\nThat way the logic is a lot clearer - either we\u0027re done, we queue, or we do an action.",
